model_response:
It seems like you are not setting up the navigation properly in your Routes component. The issue might be occurring because you have not added the navigation links to navigate to different paths in your layout component. 

To fix this, you can add the navigation links inside the Layout component and render them in the Header component. Here is an example of how you can modify your code:

1. Modify your Layout component to include navigation links:

```javascript
import React from 'react';
import { Link } from 'react-router-dom';

const Layout = () => {
  return (
    <div>
      <Header>
        <nav>
          <ul>
            <li><Link to="/">Home</Link></li>
            <li><Link to="/Test">Test</Link></li>
          </ul>
        </nav>
      </Header>
      <Content>
        {/* content goes here */}
      </Content>
      <Footer>
        {/* footer goes here */}
      </Footer>
    </div>
  );
}

export default Layout;
```

2. Modify your App component to render the Layout component instead of just the Layout element:

```javascript
function App() {
  return (
    <BrowserRouter>
      <Routes>
        <Route path="/" element={<Layout />} />
        <Route index element={<Home />} />
        <Route path="/Test" element={<ExampleComponent />} />
      </Routes>
    </BrowserRouter>
  );
}
```

By adding the navigation links inside your Layout component and rendering them in the Header component, you should now see the navigation links on all paths, not just the root path.

